  <Document>
    <name>🌞 LIVE SOLAR RADIATION</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE SOLAR RADIATION</h2><p><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-22 11:00 UTC<br/><b>Source updated:</b> n/a (NOMADS)<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-22 12:34 UTC<br/><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/solar_radiation/legend.png?v=2026-09-22_1234_UTC" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Surface downward shortwave solar radiation (W/m^2, hourly-averaged for the analysis hour), balanced linear scale: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (dark blue) → common 0 → <b>HIGHEST+ 787.6</b> (deep purple). Values shown exactly as observed; night reads zero; clouds reduce values quantitatively. Broadband flux, not the UV index.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km surface analysis, DSWRF (downward short-wave radiation flux), hourly cycles<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_hrrr_2d.pl">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_hrrr_2d.pl</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE SOLAR RADIATION</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h2>LIVE SOLAR RADIATION</h2><p>Surface downward shortwave solar radiation flux: solar power arriving at the surface, hourly-averaged for the model analysis hour. Nighttime reads zero (valid data, deep blue) — not missing data. Clouds reduce values quantitatively versus clear sky.</p><p><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/solar_radiation/legend.png?v=2026-09-22_1234_UTC" width="600" alt="key"></p><p>Surface downward shortwave solar radiation (W/m^2, hourly-averaged for the analysis hour), balanced linear scale: <b>LOWEST 0</b> (dark blue) → common 0 → <b>HIGHEST+ 787.6</b> (deep purple). Values shown exactly as observed; night reads zero; clouds reduce values quantitatively. Broadband flux, not the UV index.</p><p><b>Variable:</b> DSWRF surface analysis step (hourly-averaged downward shortwave flux for the analysis hour)<br/><b>Units:</b> W/m^2 (hourly-averaged flux for the analysis hour (not instantaneous, not daily accumulation))<br/><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km surface analysis, DSWRF (downward short-wave radiation flux), hourly cycles<br/><b>Update:</b> hourly analysis cycles<br/><b>Data time:</b> 2026-09-22 11:00 UTC<br/><b>Processed:</b> 2026-09-22 12:34 UTC<br/><b>Provenance:</b> <a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_hrrr_2d.pl">NOMADS HRRR</a></p>]]></description>
